{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'git diff --stat && git diff -- src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj test/yang/clojure_test.clj'","aggregated_output":" src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc      | 130 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------\n test/yang/clojure_test.clj      |  65 ++++++++++++++++++--\n test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj |   8 ++-\n 3 files changed, 177 insertions(+), 26 deletions(-)\ndiff --git a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\nindex f33efa87..59512a68 100644\n--- a/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n+++ b/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc\n@@ -27,7 +27,9 @@\n   as regular function applications and resolved through the module system at runtime.\n \n   The compiler is written in .cljc format to run on both JVM and Node.js.\"\n-  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile]))\n+  (:refer-clojure :exclude [compile])\n+  (:require [yang.core.call :as call]\n+            [yang.core.uast :as u]))\n \n \n ;; Forward declaration for mutual recursion\n@@ -615,10 +617,10 @@\n ;;\n ;; Lowering is a source-to-source pass over one function body, run before the\n ;; ordinary compile. A tail form returns an outcome: a value is wrapped, a\n-;; guest call in tail position is forwarded UNCHANGED (no let, no test, so the\n-;; semantic VM's return stack stays constant through tail chains), `throw`\n-;; becomes the error outcome. A may-fail form in operand position is the early\n-;; return pattern, the only mechanism:\n+;; plain private closure call in tail position is forwarded unchanged, and a\n+;; descriptor call passes through the common entry/raise bridge before its\n+;; normal value becomes an ok outcome. `throw` becomes the error outcome. A\n+;; may-fail form in operand position is the early return pattern:\n ;;\n ;;   (let [o <outcome>] (if (error? o) o <rest of the function with (payload o)>))\n ;;\n@@ -1016,9 +1018,53 @@\n     (check-binder! p params)))\n \n \n+(defn- outcome-node\n+  